# Master App Design Prompt – PGA TOUR 2K25 Golf Course Designer Studio



Windows desktop application

AI-assisted design

LiDAR & terrain mapping



## 1. Project vision

Design and develop a sophisticated Windows desktop application called 2K25 Golf Course Designer Studio.

The application's purpose is to act as an intelligent planning, visualisation and design companion for people creating golf courses using the Course Designer in PGA TOUR 2K25.

It should help users progress from an initial creative idea to a detailed, practical golf course design that can be recreated inside the game.

The application must combine:

- AI-powered golf course concept generation.
- Environment and landscape visualisation.
- Real-world golf course research.
- LiDAR terrain data processing and heightmap preparation.
- OpenStreetMap integration.
- Golf hole routing and layout planning.
- Terrain and elevation analysis.
- Individual hole design tools.
- Bunker, green, fairway and hazard planning.
- Planting and environmental design.
- Course architecture recommendations.
- Design execution instructions for PGA TOUR 2K25.
- Project management and design documentation.

Important design principle: This is not intended to replace the in-game Course Designer. It is an external design studio that helps users plan, prepare, visualise, organise and execute their ideas more efficiently.

The application should support both:

1. Creative course design: Inventing entirely fictional golf courses with unique environments, themes and architectural concepts.
2. Real-world course recreation: Using geographical information, LiDAR elevation data, mapping information and reference imagery to recreate real golf courses as accurately as possible.

The application should be designed for Windows 10 and Windows 11 desktop computers, with local project storage and an interface optimised for mouse, keyboard and large desktop monitors.

