## 6.2 LiDAR processing workflow

Create a guided workflow with the following stages.

Stage 1 – Import source data

- Select LiDAR files.
- Import the target golf course location.
- Import OpenStreetMap data.
- Identify coordinate reference systems.
- Display data coverage.
- Check file completeness.

Stage 2 – Coordinate reference system

Automatically identify the coordinate reference system (CRS) where possible.

Allow users to manually select an EPSG code.

Display:

- Current CRS.
- Horizontal coordinate system.
- Vertical datum.
- Elevation units.
- Geographic projection.
- Conversion status.

The application must warn users about mismatched horizontal and vertical reference systems.

Stage 3 – Point-cloud processing

Provide options to:

- Filter unwanted points.
- Remove noise.
- Separate ground and non-ground returns.
- Generate ground-only point clouds.
- Identify vegetation.
- Identify buildings.
- Identify roads.
- Identify water features.
- Create a digital terrain model (DTM).
- Create a digital surface model (DSM).

Prioritise ground elevation data for golf course terrain recreation.

Stage 4 – Heightmap generation

Generate heightmaps from the processed elevation information.

Options:

- Resolution selection.
- Elevation range.
- Minimum and maximum elevation.
- Vertical exaggeration.
- Smoothing.
- Noise reduction.
- Terrain cropping.
- Boundary masking.
- Elevation normalisation.

Allow the user to inspect the resulting heightmap before proceeding.

Stage 5 – Terrain mask editing

Include a visual mask editor.

Allow users to:

- Paint unwanted areas.
- Remove surrounding terrain.
- Define course boundaries.
- Highlight areas to retain.
- Mask roads and buildings.
- Select terrain regions.
- Preview the retained area.

Use clear colour-coded masking and provide undo/redo.

Stage 6 – OpenStreetMap integration

Import geographical features from OpenStreetMap.

Recognise and display:

- Roads.
- Buildings.
- Waterways.
- Lakes.
- Woodland.
- Paths.
- Land boundaries.
- Other useful geographical features.

Allow users to select which features to retain, discard or use as reference overlays.

Stage 7 – Terrain preview

Display the processed terrain in an interactive 3D environment.

Include:

- Rotatable camera.
- Zoom.
- Elevation shading.
- Contour lines.
- Heightmap overlay.
- Course boundary.
- Water features.
- OSM reference overlay.
- Terrain exaggeration controls.

Stage 8 – Export preparation

Prepare terrain information for the selected PGA TOUR 2K25 import workflow.

Provide:

- Processed heightmap.
- Terrain mask.
- Coordinate information.
- OSM data.
- Terrain preview.
- Processing report.
- Export compatibility report.

